      {
        "date": "2026-09-02",
        "change": "take_all_qualified true, max_concurrent 6 (version 1.1.0)",
        "rationale": "The one-per-day pick has no measured skill (tiebreaker spearman +0.035; skipped > picked on 8/17 and again on 9/02 clean: PICKED R +0.023 vs SKIPPED +0.518, p=0.908; no entry metric separates winners from losers on 14 live or 43 historical). The edge is the screen, not the choosing, so discarding ~60% of qualified names was throwing away return. Take-all at equal weight looked better on the same small cohort (the '~16x Sharpe-ish' figure once quoted here is WITHDRAWN 2026-10-04: a ratio of small-sample estimates with a near-zero denominator, not a portfolio Sharpe). Gates, exits, thresholds unchanged. Cap 6 covers 94% of days (median 2 open). Position size = 1/6 of book. Also triples the learning sample."
      },
      {
        "date": "2026-10-04",
